A||||3||Cliff Pennock||Question about DVD repair||||1||
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||10-14-2000||05:29 AM||||I've tried the sci.electronics.* newsgroups a few times - not a single answer. I've tried the creative.* newsgroups - not a single reply. So I'll try the Fiero Forum instead.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>My Creative Labs 2x PC-DVD player died on me a few weeks ago. Since I hate throwing stuff away just because they don't work, I opened it up to see if I could find anything wrong with it. At first I couldn't and out of pure frustration I started fiddling with the pots on the optical pickup (I know, bad idea). Ofcourse that didn't help. Then I suddenly saw what was wrong; one of the magnets of the focus-servo had come loose and was preventing the lens from focusing. I glued the magnet back on and now the player is able to recognize ordinary CDs but no DVDs, probably because I have been fiddling with the pots. I know one pot is the laser-power adjustment but I have no clue what the other is (tracking servo adjustment?). The optical pickup is from Sanyo (I know that much) but I do not know a part number. I've been searching the net - including all Sanyo/Fisher sites - for datasheets but couldn't find any.<P>So my question is: does anyone know how I can get my hands on a service-manual for this particular PC-DVD player? Or does anyone know where I can find datasheets for the Sanyo optical pickup? Or are there people here with experience in adjusting optical pickups? For instance, I know how to adjust the laser-power - by connecting a scope to the RF testpoints and adjusting the "eye-pattern". But how about stuff like focussing, tracking, etc.?<P>Anyone?<P>(PS: I know it's easier and cheaper to just buy me a new player, but that wouldn't be as much fun now, would it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fearless Freep||10-14-2000||08:19 AM||||I tried working on one of the Toshiba DVD players once...had pretty much the same problems.....except for the case, the man that needed the work done had his computer smacked with a baseball bat by his landlord.  Could never find a repair manual on those suckers, probably something to do with the company not wanting hacks like us radiating our brains or something.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>However, you may be able to find something at this website....they have a slew of articles and deal with nothing but DVD stuff. <A HREF="http://www.dvdutils.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dvdutils.com</A> <P>Its been about 8 months since I have been to that site....not quite sure how it is anymore. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fearless Freep||10-14-2000||08:32 AM||||Might also be able to find something here: <A HREF="http://www.repairfaq.org/sam/odfaq.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.repairfaq.org/sam/odfaq.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||HELI FLYER||10-14-2000||11:50 AM||||Cliff i would send it off to be recalibrated do to the pots being tweeked. The votage setings and adjustments are way out! Sending it to the manuf. is a lot cheaper then buying a new one :0<P>------------------<BR>WILL TRADE WIFE FOR 88 GT<p>[This message has been edited by HELI FLYER (edited 10-14-2000).]||||reg||6
